0. NAMING NOTE (no silent drift)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The `ClimatePanel*` Swift type namespace is already owned by the existing
dashboard-widget `TeslaSync/dashboard-widgets/ClimateControlPanelWidget.*`
(ClimatePanelModel, ClimatePanelProjection, ClimatePanelTemperatureUnit,
ClimatePanelSource, ClimatePanelStrings, ClimatePanelAccessibility, …) in the
SAME `TeslaSync` module. To stay collision-free this surface prefixes every public
type with `CabinClimate*` (View `CabinClimatePanel`). The file names remain
`ClimatePanel.*` (allowed-files + commit scope) and the P1/S11 diagnostics surface
slug remains the literal "ClimatePanel" (CabinClimateSurface.slug).

Files shipped (9):
  ClimatePanel.swift            — the surface View (FadeIn + GlassPanel + header + body)
  ClimatePanel.Adapter.swift    — snapshot, temp unit + SI convert, formatter, chip value types
  ClimatePanel.Projector.swift  — projection + builder, phase, freshness chip, accessibility
  ClimatePanel.Model.swift      — telemetry seam, outcome, source seam, @Observable model, i18n facade
  ClimatePanel.Views.swift      — header, body, content, metric tiles, rows, fan gauge, status chip
  ClimatePanel.StateViews.swift — flow layout, skeleton, stale/offline banner, error, empty
  ClimatePanel.Previews.swift   — 7 previews (loading/loaded/loaded°F/empty/error/stale/offline)
  ClimatePanel.strings          — P1/S10 i18n catalog (web parity keys + native chrome)
  ClimatePanel.Tests.swift      — adapter + projection + accessibility + model tests

